# Format before handoff and commit

Run team formatters on **changed paths only** before **handing off** work or **creating a commit**.

## When to run

| Trigger | Run formatters? |
|---------|-----------------|
| **Hand off** — complete ticket, close issue, post test plan, end implementation turn without further code planned | **Yes** |
| **Commit** — user asks to create a commit or commit and push | **Yes** (skip if already formatted this session and `git diff` unchanged) |
| Mid-implementation, user still iterating | No — unless they ask |

Handoff happens **before** test-plan comments, fresh-reviewer (when required), and commit. Commit workflow still formats if handoff was skipped.

## Repos and file types

| Repo | `.cs` (CSharpier) | `.uxml` / `.uss` (Prettier) |
|------|-------------------|-----------------------------|
| **griddungeon-game** | Yes | Yes (`Assets/**/*.uxml`, `Assets/**/*.uss`) |
| **griddungeon-design-docs** | Skip (no game C#) | Skip |

Skip when the change set has **no** paths for that formatter.

## Procedure (agents)

1. `git status` + `git diff` — list every changed `.cs`, `.uxml`, and `.uss` (staged + unstaged) under the task scope.
2. If none, skip.
3. From **griddungeon-game** root, in order:
   - **CSharpier** on changed `.cs` — skill **csharpier-format**:
     ```powershell
     dotnet tool restore
     dotnet csharpier format path/to/Changed.cs
     ```
   - **Prettier** on changed `.uxml` and `.uss` — skill **prettier-uitk-format**:
     ```powershell
     npm install
     npx prettier --write path/to/Changed.uxml path/to/Changed.uss
     ```
4. Re-run `git diff`. Include formatting-only changes in the handoff tree or commit unless the user excludes them.
5. **Verify `using` directives** on every changed `.cs` — `unity-common-pitfalls.mdc` § Handoff — **missing** imports (mirror sibling `using` lines) and **duplicate** identical `using` lines (remove extras); run `Tools/request-compile-status.ps1` when Editor may be open — see `unity-compile-status-agent.mdc`.

## Editor parity

- **C#:** CSharpier extension (`csharpier.csharpier-vscode`) — should match CLI.
- **UXML / USS:** Prettier extension (`esbenp.prettier-vscode`) — should match CLI (`.prettierrc`; `*.uss` associated as CSS in `.vscode/settings.json`).

## If CLI is unavailable

Do not substitute another formatter. Ask the user to format the listed files in Cursor (**Format Document**), then re-check `git diff`.

## Exceptions

- User explicitly requests **skip format** or **commit without formatting**.

## Out of scope

- Shaders, YAML, `.md` — not covered by this rule.
